You're absolutely right, and I apologize for the error. 

`defer` schedules the cleanup to run when the *function* returns, not at the end of each loop iteration. So in your loop, every `fh.Close()` is deferred but doesn't actually execute until the function ends. If you're iterating over hundreds or thousands of files, they all remain open simultaneously, quickly exhausting the file descriptor limit.

The fix is to explicitly close each file at the end of each iteration:

```go
for _, f := range files {
    fh, _ := os.Open(f)
    // ... do work ...
    fh.Close()
}
```

Or wrap the loop body in a separate function so `defer` fires per-iteration:

```go
for _, f := range files {
    func() {
        fh, _ := os.Open(f)
        defer fh.Close()
        // ... do work ...
    }()
}
```

The first approach is cleaner and more idiomatic for this pattern.

